Event will start on July the 1st! \n\ud83d\udd2b 4 Fresh new weapon skins per suit to show off your style.\n\ud83c\udfa8 New crosshair colour customization with a shared palette and an in game colour dial, plus a toggle to switch the lock on target markers on or off.\n\n\u2699\ufe0f Improvements\n\n\ud83d\udc7e Enemies keep firing and tracking you even while being knocked back, and Sentry Stalk and Sentinel knockback behaviour has been reworked for fairer fights.\n\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f The Sentry Stalk now roams a wider and deeper area, and the Drill Rocket has been improved.\n\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Fixed the Goliath shield glow and polished several weapon skins.\n\ud83c\udfaf Improved long range aim so the reticle lines up with where your shot actually lands.\n\ud83d\udeec Smoother landing and takeoff portals.\n\ud83d\ude81 The hub dropship now leaves the drop off point faster.\n\ud83d\udccf Improved height calibration so your view sits at the correct eye height even when headset tracking struggles.\n\ud83d\udd0a Boosted NPC dialogue volume so voices come through clearly. [Quest]\n\n\ud83d\udc1b Bug Fixes\n\n\ud83d\udcbe Fixed missing New Game Plus button and hub vendor in the Aftermath area for rare save issues.\n\ud83e\ude91 Fixed co-op seating not syncing and players getting stranded in the dropship during drop off.\n\ud83d\ude81 Fixed the dropship appearing in the hub by mistake, and it now departs correctly at mission end even with the door closed.\n\ud83e\uddf1 Fixed holes appearing in level geometry caused by faces being hidden incorrectly.\n\u2615 Hub shop props such as mugs now react much better to explosions.\n\ud83c\udfa8 Fixed a shader issue that ignored Base Color tint on certain surfaces.\n\ud83e\udd98 Fixed a jump issue where it sometimes does not detect.\n", "created_date": 1782242403, "id": "36613974361551208", "version": "1.14.17", "version_code": 627, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary":